{"availability":"available","full":"stanford-oval/storm","name":"storm","description":"An LLM-powered knowledge curation system that researches a topic and generates a full-length report with citations.","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":31562,"forks":2974,"created":"2024-03-24T16:23:39Z","updated":"2025-09-30T18:07:21Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"http://storm.genie.stanford.edu","topics":["agentic-rag","deep-research","emnlp2024","knowledge-curation","large-language-models","naacl","nlp","report-generation","retrieval-augmented-generation"],"demo":null,"color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T21:19:25.187Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-03T21:19:25.187Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-03T21:19:25.187Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T21:19:25.187Z","stars":31562,"forks":2974}],"technologies":["Python"],"lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T09:39:19.480Z","enrichmentAttemptAt":"2026-10-03T05:38:03.134Z","latestRelease":{"name":"v1.1.0 Compatible with LiteLLM API","tag":"v1.1.0","publishedAt":"2025-01-23T07:21:44Z","url":"https://github.com/stanford-oval/storm/releases/tag/v1.1.0"},"releaseCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T05:38:03.134Z","screenshots":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["STORM is a LLM system that writes Wikipedia-like articles from scratch based on Internet search. Co-STORM further enhanced its feature by enabling human to collaborative LLM system to support more aligned and preferred information seeking and knowledge curation.","While the system cannot produce publication-ready articles that often require a significant number of edits, experienced Wikipedia editors have found it helpful in their pre-writing stage.","More than 70,000 people have tried our live research preview. Try it out to see how STORM can help your knowledge exploration journey and please provide feedback to help us improve the system 🙏!"],"features":["[2025/01] We add litellm integration for language models and embedding models in knowledge-storm v1.1.0.","[2024/09] We introduce collaborative STORM (Co-STORM) to support human-AI collaborative knowledge curation! Co-STORM Paper has been accepted to EMNLP 2024 main conference.","[2024/07] We add VectorRM to support grounding on user-provided documents, complementing existing support of search engines (YouRM, BingSearch). (check out #58)","[2024/07] We release demo light for developers a minimal user interface built with streamlit framework in Python, handy for local development and demo hosting (checkout #54)","[2024/06] We will present STORM at NAACL 2024! Find us at Poster Session 2 on June 17 or check our presentation material."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/stanford-oval/storm/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"711016d02ae72a43ae96198ede47ee0b36ab10029b323a76eb2d3cd87413e2a2","extractedAt":"2026-10-03T06:15:32.414Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T09:39:19.476Z","overviewRepoUpdated":"2025-09-30T18:07:21Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"STORM is a LLM system that writes Wikipedia-like articles from scratch based on Internet search. Co-STORM further enhanced its feature by enabling human to collaborative LLM system to support more aligned and preferred information seeking and knowledge curation.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/stanford-oval/storm/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"api_key","status":"required","text":"We suggest using secrets.toml to set up the API keys.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/stanford-oval/storm/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"711016d02ae72a43ae96198ede47ee0b36ab10029b323a76eb2d3cd87413e2a2","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/stanford-oval/storm/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-03T09:39:19.477Z"},"readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/stanford-oval/storm/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-03T16:23:45.192Z","hash":"711016d02ae72a43ae96198ede47ee0b36ab10029b323a76eb2d3cd87413e2a2","originalBytes":20091,"stored